Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 17:08:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 68/74] Song browser: the audio serviced while its window is
 sorted; fewer reads stepping up

With a song playing, scrolling the song browser on the emulator (a typical
card, 1 ms per command; a folder of 1,200 songs with a group of 120 versions;
20 ms between steps) left the audio routine waiting up to 1.2 ms (v16:
0.4 ms), the DMA up to 102 samples behind (v16: 57), over 64 samples 480
times (v16: never): every cull while the folder is read sorts the window,
100 file items instead of 20, 1 ms of strcmpspecial() without the audio
routine. The sort now runs it before each partition of 24 items or more,
only for a window larger than the other browsers' (the song browser's);
stepping over a folded group's versions runs it every 16 steps.

Stepping up read the folder twice every 3 steps: the read reaching back
from the window's first item ended right after the selection, so the rows
below it weren't in the window and were read again, which left the
selection near the window's start again. That read now ends with the rows
below the selection: 14 reads for 600 steps (was 201; v16: 180).

Now across the group and back: 6 reads (v16: 68), the audio routine
waiting at most 390 us (v16: 396), the DMA at most 39 samples behind (v16:
57); across 300 files and back: 14 reads, 320 us, 48 samples (v16: 180,
382 us, 55); no underruns in either.

